  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">JPO JPOSC 2024 - JPO JPOSC 2024 Ny strategi</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">JPO JPOSC 2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Bidra till genomf&#xf6;randet av Agenda 2030 genom att tillhandah&#xe5;lla personal inom
prioriterade &#xe4;mnesomr&#xe5;den.

Bidra till delm&#xe5;len inom Strategin f&#xf6;r kapacitetsutveckling, partnerskap och
metoder som st&#xf6;djer Agenda 2030 f&#xf6;r h&#xe5;llbar utveckling 20182022 (f&#xf6;rl&#xe4;ngd t o
m 20240331), som syftar till en bredare svensk resursbas genom att:

1) &#xd6;ka svensk representation p&#xe5; strategiska tj&#xe4;nster i internationellt
utvecklingssamarbete.

2) &#xd6;ka anv&#xe4;ndning och &#xe5;terf&#xf6;ring av svensk kompetens och erfarenhet inom
internationellt utvecklingssamarbete

Insatsen avser f&#xf6;ljande tj&#xe4;nster:

1. UNCDF  Strategic Programme and Innovation Analyst, Nature and Asset Team (NAT), Kigali, Rwanda.

2. UNDP  Stabilization Officer, Peace &amp; Security, Kinshasa, DR Kongo.

3. UNDP  Climate Support Officer, Climate, Belgrade, Serbia.

4. UNDP  Disaster Risk Reduction Analyst, M &amp; E, Skopje, North Macedonia.

5. UNDP  Programme analyst, Effective Governance, Governance, Chisinau, Moldova.

6. UNFPA  Innovation and Knowledge Management Sexual and Reproductive Health, SRHR, Pretoria, South Africa.

7. UN Women  Communications &amp; Data Analyst, Comm &amp; Data, Kiev, Ukraine.

8. UN Women  Monitoring &amp; Evaluation Analyst, M &amp; E, New York, USA.

9. WHO  Technical Officer (sexual, reproductive, maternal, newborn, child and adolescent health SRMNCAH), Health/SRHR, Kampala, Uganda.

10. WHO  Technical Officer (Climate change and capacity strengthening) Health,
Geneva, Switzerland.

11. UNDP Regional youth civic engagement and governance officer, Amman,
Jordan.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen bidrar till Sveriges &#xe5;tagande att bidra till genomf&#xf6;randet av Agenda 2030 i utvecklingsl&#xe4;nder genom att tillhandah&#xe5;lla personal som arbetar med och genom FN organens och V&#xe4;rldsbankens olika mandat. F&#xf6;r detta &#xe4;ndam&#xe5;l har Sverige ett n&#xe4;ra samarbete med FN:s utvecklings; humanit&#xe4;ra och fredsbevarande pelare med placeringar runt om i v&#xe4;rlden. 

Insatsen bidrar &#xe4;ven till Strategin f&#xf6;r kapacitetsutveckling, partnerskap och metoder som st&#xf6;djer Agenda 2030 f&#xf6;r h&#xe5;llbar utveckling 2018-2022 (f&#xf6;rl&#xe4;ngd t o m 31 mars 2024). 

Tj&#xe4;nsterna som ska finansieras &#xe4;r som f&#xf6;ljer:
UNCDF &#xac; Strategic Programme and Innovation Analyst, Nature and Asset Team (NAT), Kigali, Rwanda. 
UNDP &#xac; Stabilization Officer, Peace &amp; Security, Kinshasa, DR Kongo. 
UNDP &#xac; Climate Support Officer, Climate, Belgrade, Serbia. 
UNDP &#xac; Disaster Risk Reduction Analyst, M &amp; E, Skopje, North Macedonia. 
UNDP &#xac; Programme analyst, Effective Governance, Governance, Chisinau, Moldova. 
UNFPA &#xac; Innovation and Knowledge Management Sexual and Reproductive Health, SRHR, Pretoria, South Africa. 
UN Women &#xac; Communications &amp; Data Analyst, Comm &amp; Data, Kiev, Ukraine. 
UN Women &#xac; Monitoring &amp; Evaluation Analyst, M &amp; E, New York, USA. 
WHO &#xac; Technical Officer (sexual, reproductive, maternal, newborn, child and adolescent health SRMNCAH), Health/SRHR, Kampala, Uganda. 
WHO &#xac; Technical Officer (Climate change and capacity strengthening) Health, Geneva, Switzerland.
Se bilagda arbetsbeskrivningar f&#xf6;r mer information</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sweden is committed to contribute to the implementation of Agenda 2030 in developing countries by providing human resources to work with and through the diverse mandates of UN agencies, funds and programmes, as well as the World Bank. for this purpose, Sweden closely collaborates with the UN development, humanitarian and peacekeeping pillars with placements around the world. 

The contribution further aims at fulfilling the Strategy for capacity development, partnerships and methods that support the 2030 Agenda for sustainable development 2018-2022 (extended until 31 March 2024). 

The JPO positions to be finances are as follows: 

UNCDF - Strategic Programme and Innovation Analyst, Nature and Asset Team (NAT), Kigali, Rwanda. 
UNDP - Stabilization Officer, Peace &amp; Security, Kinshasa, DR Kongo. 
UNDP - Climate Support Officer, Climate, Belgrade, Serbia. 
UNDP - Disaster Risk Reduction Analyst, M &amp; E, Skopje, North Macedonia. 
UNDP - Programme analyst, Effective Governance, Governance, Chisinau, Moldova. 
UNFPA - Innovation and Knowledge Management Sexual and Reproductive Health, SRHR, Pretoria, South Africa. 
UN Women - Communications &amp; Data Analyst, Comm &amp; Data, Kiev, Ukraine. 
UN Women - Monitoring &amp; Evaluation Analyst, M &amp; E, New York, USA. 
WHO - Technical Officer (sexual, reproductive, maternal, newborn, child and adolescent health SRMNCAH), Health/SRHR, Kampala, Uganda. 
WHO - Technical Officer (Climate change and capacity strengthening) Health, Geneva, Switzerland.</narrative>
  </description>
